### SECTION C: TECHNOLOGY & ARCHITECTURE

**10. Proposed Stack: Headless (Next.js + Headless CMS)**  
* **Why NOT WordPress:** Vulnerable to security breaches, slow plugin bloat, frequent database exploits, and high maintenance overhead.
* **Why NOT Webflow:** High recurring lock-in fees, limited custom backend API integration, and restricted local payment flexibility.
* **The Choice (Headless Next.js 15 + Headless CMS):** Unmatched speed, enterprise-grade edge security (no publicly exposed database), full API adaptability, and modular 5-year scalability with zero licensing lock-in.

**11. Asset Ownership & Credentials (Day One)**  
Ken-Saleem Consulting Limited owns 100% of all intellectual assets from inception. The domain, hosting workspace, CMS accounts, GitHub code repository, and Figma design files are registered directly under your corporate credentials.

**12. Hosting Architecture, Uptime SLA & Backup Redundancy**  
* **Hosting:** Cloudflare Edge / Vercel Serverless CDN distributed across 300+ global edge locations.
* **Uptime SLA:** 99.99% continuous availability.
* **Backups:** Automated, immutable daily database snapshots stored on separate S3-compatible cloud object storage with a recovery time objective (RTO) of under 15 minutes.

**13. Version Control & Staging Environments**  
Zero direct-to-live deployments. We enforce a professional CI/CD pipeline via GitHub:  
Local Development -> Staging Environment (staging.ken-saleem.com) -> Client QA Sign-Off -> Automated Zero-Downtime Production Push

**14. Future-Proof API Integrations**  
The site is built as a decoupled REST/GraphQL API consumer. Native endpoints and webhooks are pre-structured to bridge CRM platforms (HubSpot, Zoho), Paystack payment webhooks, Calendly scheduling feeds, and AI conversational desks without rewriting core code.

